course: dictionary
lesson: 14900
title: Put it right
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When something is wrong, you can rectify it, which means you fix it so it is right again. Rectify is a formal word, the kind you find in letters from companies and official notices. «The error has been rectified» means the mistake was found and put right.
explain: In maths, a wrong answer must be rectified. You find the mistake in your working and correct it. Then ask: what would fit here? «Nadia rectified her sum after she spotted the missing carry digit» means she fixed her sum.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Rectified sits next to words like error, mistake or problem, and the sentence says it was fixed. Test your meaning: «The error has been fixed» still makes sense, so put right is the right meaning.
fact: Rectify means to put something right or correct it.
fact: «Rectified» is the past form of rectify: «The mistake was rectified.»
fact: Fixed and corrected have similar meanings, but rectify sounds more formal, as in letters, notices and exam questions.
fact: «The company rectified the problem within a day.» Here the company put the problem right.
fact: In science, rectified can mean changed from alternating current into direct current in electricity. This is an advanced meaning.
exercise: «The error has been rectified.» What does rectified mean here? | *Put right | Hidden away | Lost forever | Made bigger
exercise: «Ben found the missing digit and rectified his sum.» What did Ben do to his sum? | Added more numbers to it | Rubbed it out and left it blank | *Corrected it | Shouted at it
exercise: Which word means the same as rectified? | Painted | Broken | Forgotten | *Fixed
test: «The problem was quickly rectified by the shop.» What does this tell you? | The problem got worse | The shop closed for the day | *The shop put the problem right | The shop sold more toys
test: «Mum asked us to rectify our mistake on the spelling list.» What should we do? | Add more mistakes to it | Read the list aloud only | Hide the list under the bed | *Correct the mistake
exam: In «The company rectified the faulty phone», what does rectified mean? | Delayed for a week | Thrown away | Sold cheaply | *Put right
